/-!
# The standard integer generator matrix of the Leech lattice

The Leech lattice `Λ₂₄ ⊂ ℝ²⁴` has a standard generator matrix whose `24` rows, after division by
`√8`, form a `ℤ`-basis of `Λ₂₄` in Conway–Sloane's (MOG) coordinate order; these coordinates differ
from those of other Golay-code models of `Λ₂₄` by a permutation of `Fin 24`.  This file records the
integer matrix `M` with those rows (before the `√8` scaling) and computes its determinant.

The matrix is lower triangular with diagonal
`8, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 2, 4, 4, 4, 2, 4, 2, 2, 2, 4, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1`, so
`det M = 2 ^ 36 = 8 ^ 12`.  Since dividing all `24` rows by `√8` multiplies the determinant by
`(√8)⁻²⁴ = 8⁻¹²`, the scaled basis has determinant `1`, so the lattice spanned by the scaled rows
has covolume `1`.

## Main definitions and results

* `SphereCeti.Leech.basisCoordinateMatrix`: the integer matrix `M`.
* `SphereCeti.Leech.basisCoordinateMatrix_def`, `SphereCeti.Leech.basisCoordinateMatrix_apply`:
  the explicit rows and entries of `M`.
* `SphereCeti.Leech.basisCoordinateMatrix_isLowerTriangular`: `M` is lower triangular.
* `SphereCeti.Leech.basisCoordinateMatrix_det`: `det M = 8 ^ 12`.

## References

* J. H. Conway and N. J. A. Sloane, *Sphere Packings, Lattices and Groups*, 3rd ed., Springer
  (1999), Chapter 4, §11, Figure 4.12: the standard generator matrix of the Leech lattice, scaled
  by `√8`.  The entries of `basisCoordinateMatrix` are transcribed from this figure.

No proof text is adapted from another source.
-/

